    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b9db05d6adf0c93750466ae8d2685927adf5d5fedb44203f71ec3d914b26ecd1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The admissible-polynomial problem is made computational by composing two representations: the class P_n supplies the analytic objective and its coefficient constraints, while the squared-exponential parameterization makes global nonnegativity automatic and expresses the remaining tests and Landau objective through finitely many autocorrelations that can be updated during annealing.",
